From 84ca6d166fa7afed8d15b164d132e6b15b699058 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 20:48:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02934/11362] [outer-loop] (a) revise .414 roadmap: lead with
 score-drivers (integration + verifier-discrimination)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reprioritized per the step-back gap audit. The 4 leading tasks are now the actual leaderboard
score-movers (reproducible_total_levels is a mirage for scoring):
- A1: wire the stronger generic stack (router + world-model-DSL) into the SUBMITTED agent (today
  bare BFS 8/32 in-dist/~0 OOD) + raise target_levels + forward-edge nav [GAP-LIVE-INTEGRATION]
- A2: verifier features v3 (relational/Δframe/action-conditioned) -> fix the cross-game LOO-AUROC
  0.503 chance [GAP-ARCH-FEATURES]
- A3: wire the shipped per-game online discriminative head to prune traps
- A4: E3 goal-predicate verification + (grid,registers) HUD state for the deepening tail
Public-25 closeout (re86/bp35/lf52) kept for the level-up guarantee; infra/hardware/SOTA reserved.
12 tasks, all codex, level-up lint passes (2>=1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
